# std/diff — one of the history tools (std/git-history holds the source they share).
# The help is a HERE-STRING so it lives in this expression, which is stripped
# from the tree the build sees: editing the docs re-keys this tool's ArgTree and
# nothing it builds from.
HELP=<<END
Unified diff between two revisions of a source tree, optionally scoped to a path. Defaults compare the previous commit to the source tree's own (what the latest step changed). `from` and `to` accept a commit hash, HEAD with ~N or ^ ancestry, or the path of another source tree in the conversation (such as sources/foo/00-base), which compares two source trees directly.
@param source-tree Path of the source tree (a code reference in the conversation), such as feature/01-change.
@param [from] The base revision (default HEAD~1, the commit before the source tree's own), or the path of a source tree.
@param [to] The revision to compare against the base (default HEAD, the source tree's own commit), or the path of a source tree.
@param [path] Restrict the diff to this source-tree-relative path.
@in
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-history --dep0:@=DEEP-DEPS/conversation-protocol --dep1:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-locator --output-runner:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-runner
curry --base=$IMAGE --op=diff --help=$HELP
